# Tests for the Hsa module

Run with `clerk test`. Named scopes with the concrete cases of issue #35,
worked out by hand from Form 8889 (2024) and its instructions
(`sources/forms-instructions/f8889--2024.pdf`, `i8889--2024.pdf`) and Rev.
Proc. 2023-23 ($4,150 self-only, $8,300 family, $1,000 catch-up). The oracle
comparison is `make difftest SCOPE=hsa`.

> Using Types
> Using Hsa as H

## Helper: a return with defaults

By default: a single filer aged 40 with a self-only HDHP for the whole year,
no Medicare, no other coverage, no W-2 HSA contributions, no dependents, and
$0 of contributions of his own (`p_ty`, `p_ty1`). `p_made` says the filer
answers that he made contributions of his own. The spouse has the same
defaults and is only read on a joint return. Each test overrides the contexts
it needs.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context is_mfj content boolean
  context is_married content boolean
  context p_age55 content boolean
  context s_age55 content boolean
  context p_claimed content boolean
  context p_w2 content money
  context s_w2 content money
  context p_made content boolean
  context s_made content boolean
  context p_ty content money
  context p_ty1 content money
  context s_ty content money
  context s_ty1 content money
  context p_type content H.TypeOfHdhp
  context s_type content H.TypeOfHdhp
  context p_medicare content H.MedicareEnrollment
  context has_msa content boolean
  context non_w2_activity content boolean
  context p_activity content boolean
  context s_activity content boolean
  context dists content list of H.HsaDistribution
  f scope H.Hsa
  output deduction content money
  output ko_over_limit condition
  output ko_dependent condition
  output ko_medicare condition
  output ko_msa condition
  output ko_unqualified condition
  output unsupported condition
  output p_form content H.Form8889
  output s_form content H.Form8889
  output p_excess condition
  output p_exceeded_amount content money

scope Case:
  definition is_mfj equals false
  definition is_married equals false
  definition p_age55 equals false
  definition s_age55 equals false
  definition p_claimed equals false
  definition p_w2 equals $0
  definition s_w2 equals $0
  definition p_made equals true
  definition s_made equals true
  definition p_ty equals $0
  definition p_ty1 equals $0
  definition s_ty equals $0
  definition s_ty1 equals $0
  definition p_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.SelfOnly
  definition s_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.SelfOnly
  definition p_medicare equals H.MedicareEnrollment.MedicareNoneOfYear
  definition has_msa equals false
  definition non_w2_activity equals true
  definition p_activity equals true
  definition s_activity equals true
  definition dists equals []

  definition f.is_filing_status_mfj equals is_mfj
  definition f.is_married equals is_married
  definition f.is_single equals not is_married
  definition f.primary_filer_age55_or_older equals p_age55
  definition f.secondary_filer_age55_or_older equals s_age55
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals p_claimed
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s equals p_w2
  definition f.secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s equals s_w2
  definition f.has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s equals p_w2 > $0
  definition f.has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s equals s_w2 > $0
  definition f.knockout_has_no_payments_or_credits equals false
  definition f.paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year equals false
  definition f.tax_exempt_interest equals $0
  definition f.pensions_and_annuities equals $0
  definition f.social_security_benefits equals $0
  definition f.primary_filer equals H.HsaFilerAnswers {
    -- writable_primary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa: p_made
    -- writable_secondary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa: false
    -- enrolled_in_medicare: p_medicare
    -- hsa_hdhp_coverage_status: H.HdhpCoverageStatus.HdhpAllYear
    -- type_of_hdhp: p_type
    -- had_other_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa:
         H.OtherCoverageIneligible.OtherCoverageNoneOfYear
    -- writable_mfs_line6_check: false
    -- writable_change_in_marital_status_during_tax_year:
         H.MaritalStatusChange.WasNotMarriedNorDivorcedThisYear
    -- writable_marital_change_affect_contribution_limit_bool: false
    -- has_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution: false
    -- writable_hsa_nonemployer_contributions_tax_year: p_ty
    -- writable_hsa_nonemployer_contributions_tax_year_plus_one: p_ty1
  }
  definition f.secondary_filer equals H.HsaFilerAnswers {
    -- writable_primary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa: false
    -- writable_secondary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa: s_made
    -- enrolled_in_medicare: H.MedicareEnrollment.MedicareNoneOfYear
    -- hsa_hdhp_coverage_status: H.HdhpCoverageStatus.HdhpAllYear
    -- type_of_hdhp: s_type
    -- had_other_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa:
         H.OtherCoverageIneligible.OtherCoverageNoneOfYear
    -- writable_mfs_line6_check: false
    -- writable_change_in_marital_status_during_tax_year:
         H.MaritalStatusChange.WasNotMarriedNorDivorcedThisYear
    -- writable_marital_change_affect_contribution_limit_bool: false
    -- has_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution: false
    -- writable_hsa_nonemployer_contributions_tax_year: s_ty
    -- writable_hsa_nonemployer_contributions_tax_year_plus_one: s_ty1
  }
  definition f.some_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity equals non_w2_activity
  definition f.writable_primary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity equals p_activity
  definition f.writable_secondary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity equals s_activity
  definition f.has_hsa_medical_savings_account_type equals has_msa
  definition f.writable_has_hsa_excess_contributions_previous_year equals false
  definition f.writable_has_hsa_withdrawn_excess_contributions_yes_no equals false
  definition f.some_filers_made_testing_period_contribution equals false
  definition f.some_filers_have_testing_period_additional_income equals false
  definition f.hsa_distributions equals dists

  definition deduction equals f.hsa_total_deductible_amount
  rule ko_over_limit under condition f.ko_hsa_contributions_over_limit
  consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_dependent under condition f.ko_filer_is_dependent_and_contributes_to_hsa
  consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_medicare under condition
    f.ko_hsa_coverage_changing or f.ko_enrolled_in_medicare_all_year
  consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_msa under condition f.ko_hsa_medical_savings_account_type
  consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_unqualified under condition f.ko_hsa_unqualified_distributions
  consequence fulfilled
  rule unsupported under condition f.unsupported
  consequence fulfilled
  definition p_form equals f.form_8889 of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
  definition s_form equals f.form_8889 of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  rule p_excess under condition
    f.has_excess_hsa_contributions of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
  consequence fulfilled
  definition p_exceeded_amount equals
    f.hsa_contribution_limit_exceeded_amount of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
```

## Self-only coverage, full year, $4,000 of personal contributions

No employer contribution: the limit is $4,150 (line 3, line 8, line 12) and
the deduction is the smaller of line 2 and line 12, $4,000. No excess.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSelfOnly4000:
  c scope Case

scope TestSelfOnly4000:
  definition c.p_ty equals $4,000
  assertion c.deduction = $4,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_1_self_only
  assertion not c.p_form.line_1_family
  assertion c.p_form.line_2 = $4,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_3 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_5 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_6 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_7 = $0
  assertion c.p_form.line_8 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_9 = $0
  assertion c.p_form.line_11 = $0
  assertion c.p_form.line_12 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_13 = $4,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_16 = $0
  assertion not c.p_excess
  assertion not c.ko_over_limit
  assertion not c.unsupported
  # The spouse is not on the return.
  assertion c.s_form.line_13 = $0
  # The spec rejects wrong outputs.
  assertion not (c.deduction = $4,150)
  assertion not (c.deduction = $3,999)
```

Contributions for the year made by April 15 of the next year count on
line 2 (instructions line 2, `i8889--2024.pdf` p 4): $3,000 made in the year
and $1,000 made for the year in 2025 give $4,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestContributionsMadeNextYear:
  c scope Case

scope TestContributionsMadeNextYear:
  definition c.p_ty equals $3,000
  definition c.p_ty1 equals $1,000
  assertion c.deduction = $4,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_2 = $4,000
```

## $5,000 of personal contributions: limited to $4,150, excess flagged

Line 13 is capped at line 12, $4,150. The $850 above the limit is an excess
contribution (`has_excess_hsa_contributions`), which DF does not support
(`ko_hsa_contributions_over_limit`, so `unsupported`).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSelfOnly5000:
  c scope Case

scope TestSelfOnly5000:
  definition c.p_ty equals $5,000
  assertion c.deduction = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_13 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_excess
  assertion c.p_exceeded_amount = $850
  assertion c.ko_over_limit
  assertion c.unsupported
  # The bad output (the whole $5,000) is rejected.
  assertion not (c.deduction = $5,000)
```

## Age 55 or older, self-only: $5,150

Instructions line 3 (`i8889--2024.pdf` p 5): unmarried and 55 or older, add
$1,000 to line 3. Line 7 stays $0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAge55SelfOnly:
  c scope Case

scope TestAge55SelfOnly:
  definition c.p_age55 equals true
  definition c.p_ty equals $5,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_3 = $5,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_7 = $0
  assertion c.p_form.line_8 = $5,150
  assertion c.deduction = $5,150
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

## Family coverage: $8,300

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFamily:
  c scope Case

scope TestFamily:
  definition c.p_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.Family
  definition c.p_ty equals $8,300
  assertion c.p_form.line_1_family
  assertion c.p_form.line_3 = $8,300
  assertion c.p_form.line_8 = $8,300
  assertion c.deduction = $8,300
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

## Employer $3,000 plus personal $4,000 on self-only: $1,150 left

Line 9 is the W-2 box 12 code W amount, $3,000; line 12 is
$4,150 - $3,000 = $1,150 and so is the deduction. The total contributed,
$7,000, is above the $4,150 limit by $2,850.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEmployerAndPersonal:
  c scope Case

scope TestEmployerAndPersonal:
  definition c.p_w2 equals $3,000
  definition c.p_ty equals $4,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_9 = $3,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_11 = $3,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_12 = $1,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_13 = $1,150
  assertion c.deduction = $1,150
  assertion c.p_excess
  assertion c.p_exceeded_amount = $2,850
  assertion c.ko_over_limit
```

Employer contributions alone make the filer file Form 8889 but give no
deduction; they stay under the limit, so nothing is knocked out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEmployerOnly:
  c scope Case

scope TestEmployerOnly:
  definition c.p_w2 equals $3,000
  definition c.non_w2_activity equals false
  assertion c.deduction = $0
  assertion c.p_form.line_9 = $3,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_12 = $1,150
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

## Joint return

Both spouses 55 or older, married, both with family coverage, separate HSAs,
$5,000 each. Line 5 is $8,300 for each; the spouses divide it equally, $4,150
each (line 6); each adds $1,000 on line 7 (line 8 is $5,150); each deducts
$5,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjSeparateHsasFamily:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjSeparateHsasFamily:
  definition c.is_mfj equals true
  definition c.is_married equals true
  definition c.p_age55 equals true
  definition c.s_age55 equals true
  definition c.p_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.Family
  definition c.s_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.Family
  definition c.p_ty equals $5,000
  definition c.s_ty equals $5,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_5 = $8,300
  assertion c.p_form.line_6 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_7 = $1,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_8 = $5,150
  assertion c.s_form.line_6 = $4,150
  assertion c.s_form.line_8 = $5,150
  assertion c.deduction = $10,000
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

DF-BUG(7) candidate: the primary spouse put $6,000 and the secondary $1,000
into separate HSAs, both under 55 with family coverage. The law divides the
$8,300 equally unless the spouses agree on another division
(IRC 223(b)(5)(B)(ii)), so each has $4,150: the deductions are $4,150 and
$1,000. DF assumes an agreement and would give $6,000 and $1,000
(and $7,000 in total).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjEqualDivision:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjEqualDivision:
  definition c.is_mfj equals true
  definition c.is_married equals true
  definition c.p_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.Family
  definition c.s_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.Family
  definition c.p_ty equals $6,000
  definition c.s_ty equals $1,000
  assertion c.p_form.line_6 = $4,150
  assertion c.p_form.line_13 = $4,150
  assertion c.s_form.line_13 = $1,000
  assertion c.deduction = $5,150
  assertion c.p_excess
  assertion c.ko_over_limit
  assertion c.unsupported
```

Only one spouse has an HSA, with family coverage: no division, the whole
$8,300 is the limit. The spouse's answers are not read.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjOneHsa:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjOneHsa:
  definition c.is_mfj equals true
  definition c.is_married equals true
  definition c.p_type equals H.TypeOfHdhp.Family
  definition c.p_ty equals $8,300
  definition c.s_made equals false
  definition c.s_activity equals false
  assertion c.p_form.line_6 = $8,300
  assertion c.deduction = $8,300
  assertion c.s_form.line_13 = $0
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

## Knockouts

Medicare for the whole year (IRC 223(b)(7)), a dependent filer
(IRC 223(b)(6)), a medical savings account.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockouts:
  a scope Case
  b scope Case
  d scope Case
  e scope Case

scope TestKnockouts:
  definition a.p_ty equals $1,000
  definition a.p_medicare equals H.MedicareEnrollment.MedicareAllYear
  assertion a.ko_medicare
  assertion a.unsupported
  definition b.p_ty equals $1,000
  definition b.p_claimed equals true
  assertion b.ko_dependent
  assertion b.unsupported
  definition d.p_ty equals $1,000
  definition d.has_msa equals true
  assertion d.ko_msa
  assertion d.unsupported
  definition e.p_ty equals $1,000
  assertion not e.ko_medicare
  assertion not e.ko_dependent
  assertion not e.ko_msa
  assertion not e.unsupported
```

## No HSA activity

The filer answers that there are no contributions of his own and no W-2
amount: no Form 8889, deduction $0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoActivity:
  c scope Case

scope TestNoActivity:
  definition c.non_w2_activity equals false
  assertion c.deduction = $0
  assertion c.p_form.line_3 = $0
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

## Distributions (Part II)

A $900 distribution, all spent on qualified medical expenses: lines 14a, 14c,
15 are $900 and line 16 is $0 (the case in the Direct File scenario
`hsa-ats-1`). A $1,000 distribution with $900 of expenses is above the
expenses and is knocked out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDistributions:
  a scope Case
  b scope Case

scope TestDistributions:
  definition a.p_ty equals $690
  definition a.p_ty1 equals $80
  definition a.p_w2 equals $260
  definition a.dists equals [
    H.HsaDistribution {
      -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
      -- writable_distributions_rollover_bool: false
      -- writable_distributions_rollover_amount: $0
      -- writable_gross_distribution: $900
      -- has_withdrawn_excess_contributions: false
      -- writable_withdrawn_excess_contributions_amount: $0
      -- writable_earnings_on_excess_contributions: $0
      -- hsa_distribution_code: H.HsaDistributionCode.NormalDistribution
      -- writable_fmv_on_date_of_death: $0
      -- writable_qualified_med_expenses: $900
    }]
  assertion a.deduction = $770
  assertion a.p_form.line_14a = $900
  assertion a.p_form.line_14b = $0
  assertion a.p_form.line_14c = $900
  assertion a.p_form.line_15 = $900
  assertion a.p_form.line_16 = $0
  assertion not a.ko_unqualified
  assertion not a.unsupported
  definition b.p_ty equals $690
  definition b.dists equals [
    H.HsaDistribution {
      -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
      -- writable_distributions_rollover_bool: false
      -- writable_distributions_rollover_amount: $0
      -- writable_gross_distribution: $1,000
      -- has_withdrawn_excess_contributions: false
      -- writable_withdrawn_excess_contributions_amount: $0
      -- writable_earnings_on_excess_contributions: $0
      -- hsa_distribution_code: H.HsaDistributionCode.NormalDistribution
      -- writable_fmv_on_date_of_death: $0
      -- writable_qualified_med_expenses: $900
    }]
  assertion b.ko_unqualified
  assertion b.unsupported
```
